
# Where an app has been, kept across a relaunch (live reload, note/term/project/live-reload.md). The navigation
# contract (../navigation) hands its whole history here each time the app moves, and asks for it once at the start, so
# a native app rebuilt and relaunched by `term work` opens on the screen the person was looking at, with the same
# screens behind it for back.
#
# This file is the fallback for every env with no address of its own, and keeps nothing: a page has its own address bar
# and history, and the web's hot swap keeps the running app (deck/make/code/dev/client.ts), so there is nothing to
# carry. The toolkits keep it in ./toolkit/address.
#
#   restore-history   the paths kept by the run before this one, oldest first, or none
#   keep-history      the paths now, oldest first, for the next run

task restore-history
  like list
    like text
  send back
    make list

task keep-history
  take paths
    like list
      like text
  save skip, code 0
